    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=The user entered this recipe request:\n\n{{ $json.recipe }}\n\nFollow these rules carefully:\n\n1. Determine whether the user's message clearly identifies a specific recipe or dish.\nThe user may enter only the recipe name (for example, \"Tandoori Chicken\") or use a sentence such as \"I need to cook Paneer Butter Masala\". Both are valid if the intended dish is clear.\n\n2. If the input is empty, only whitespace, unclear, incomplete, unrelated to a recipe, or misspelled in a way that makes the intended recipe uncertain, reply only:\nPlease enter a clear recipe name and try again.\n\n3. Do not guess or silently correct an uncertain recipe name.\nFor example, if the user enters \"check biryani\", do not assume they meant \"chicken biryani\". Reply:\nPlease enter a clear recipe name and try again.\n\n4. If the recipe is clear, list the main products and ingredients needed to make it.\n\n5. Return a clear bulleted list with approximate quantities.\n\n6. Keep the answer short and practical.\n\n7. Do not include cooking instructions unless the user specifically asks for them.",
